From 62687f7082c2006f47e53fc3569d392b11d55bde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:18:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0121: the single-game iOS launcher in Chinese (V1.3.15)

The DmIOS launcher renders launcher.json rows verbatim, and launcher.json carries English only (dm/games/settings.py). The Mac launcher and the iOS shell translate each row at display time through the fork's l10n table (frontend/l10n/*.json), keyed launch.set.<ENV>, launch.set.<ENV>.note, launch.opt.<ENV>.<value> and launch.section.<Name>; a key the table does not have keeps the English. The DmIOS app does not bundle that table, so LauncherText.swift carries the Chinese strings itself (as \u{...} escapes: the engine writes Chinese as escapes, never as characters), generated from frontend/l10n/zh.json, and translates rows, section headings and the launcher's own chrome strings at display time, falling back to English for a row this build does not know. The model keeps the English section names, so GameMenu.swift's "Controls" match and the shared Mac window are unaffected. iPad (4:3) has no launch.opt key in zh.json; it is added here as iPad (4:3).
---
 dm/ios/Sources/GameMenu.swift     |  10 +-
 dm/ios/Sources/Launcher.swift     |  48 ++++-----
 dm/ios/Sources/LauncherRow.swift  |   2 +-
 dm/ios/Sources/LauncherText.swift | 155 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 186 insertions(+), 29 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 dm/ios/Sources/LauncherText.swift

